# Count Dominant Elements

**Problem:** [LeetCode - Count Dominant Elements](https://leetcode.com/problems/count-dominant-elements/)

## Approach: Neighbor Comparison

- Traverse the array and check each element.
- For middle elements, calculate the average of its immediate left and right neighbors.
- If the current element is greater than or equal to the average, increment the count.
- For the first and last elements, compare them with their only adjacent element.
- Return the total count.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int countDominantElements(vector<int>& nums) {
        int count = 0;
        int n = nums.size();

        if(n == 1) return 1;

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if(i != 0 && i != n-1) {
                double pivot = (nums[i-1] + nums[i+1]) / 2.0;
                if(nums[i] >= pivot) count++;
            }
            else if(i == 0 && nums[i+1] <= nums[i]) count++;
            else if(i == n-1 && nums[i-1] <= nums[i]) count++;
        }

        return count;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n) — Each element is visited exactly once.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) — No extra space is used.
